<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Italian, a draft not yet read by a fluent reviewer (#495). The notes on each string are in values/strings.xml.
    The driver is addressed as "tu". "Vehicle" is veicolo, the general word, never one kind of vehicle; "route" is linea
    (off route: fuori percorso); "run" is corsa, a timetabled departure ("la corsa delle 6:43"); "trip" is viaggio;
    "stop" is fermata; "block" is turno (short for turno macchina); "agency" is azienda; "dispatcher" is centrale
    (the control room, centrale operativa); "report" is segnalazione (feminine), and reporting is l'invio; "riders"
    are passeggeri; "driver" is autista; "schedule" and "timetable" are orario; "sign in" is Accedi, "sign out" is
    Esci, and an expired sign-in is Accesso scaduto. Dialog titles ask with an infinitive ("Terminare questo
    viaggio?"), as Android does. Plural "many" is for exact millions only, which Italian writes with "di"
    ("1.000.000 di segnalazioni").
-->
